 "license_note": "Poly Haven publishes every asset under CC0 1.0 Universal, which places the work in the public domain and permits commercial use without attribution. Attribution is not required; the author credits below are recorded as provenance only.",
 "acquired": "glTF 1k variants, downloaded per-file and md5-verified against the Poly Haven files API",
 "authoring_pipeline": "Blender 5.2.0 LTS background. Per source tree: planar dissolve then iterative collapse decimation to <=5000 triangles, trunk-base renormalisation, per-variant non-uniform proportion and lean, single UV layout, Cycles bake of diffuse/tangent-normal/roughness into one 1024px atlas, collapse to a single primitive.",
 "single_primitive_reason": "Godot MultiMesh renders surface 0 only, so a multi-material scan would draw its first material and discard the rest. Every variant is one primitive with one baked atlas material.",
 "triangle_budget": "Per-instance ceiling of 5000 triangles, chosen to keep 100940 instances inside the triangle load the previous pack occupied. The collapse decimator stalls on curve-derived topology, so the dissolve angle is ramped until each pass makes progress.",
 "known_limitations": [
  "Sixteen variants derive from six distinct scan trees (three fir, three pine, three island_tree broadleaf); silhouette variety comes from re-proportioning and lean, not from distinct source species.",
  "tree_small_02 was rejected as a seventh source: it imports as a curve-derived mesh whose boundary loops stall collapse decimation at 42494 triangles, and a weld pass reduced it less rather than more.",
  "Conifers are European/North American fir and pine. The locally correct Himalayan broadleaf and pine species have no CC0 realistic source in this pack.",
  "At 5000 triangles the silhouette carries proportion and massing, not branch or needle detail. Close views at detail_spacing_m 18 will show the limit; a per-distance LOD chain is the next lever."
 ],
